<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan unlikely to import wheat - official.</title>
<headline>Pakistan unlikely to import wheat - official.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan is unlikely to tender for an expected 100,000 tonnes of U.S. or Australian wheat this month, a Ministry of Food and Agriculture official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Import of wheat is out of the question,&quot; the official, who asked not be named, told Reuters. &quot;At this stage wheat import is not feasible.&quot;</p>
<p>The official said even if Pakistan wanted to import wheat from the United States, it would not reach port before May when a new wheat crop would start arriving in the market.</p>
<p>The official said between May and September import of wheat was not possible due to port conditions, lack of storage facilities and availability of domestic production of wheat.</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
